+\subsection*{AI disclosure}
+
+Claude Opus 5.5 discovered the normalization $N_g$ in
+Theorem~\ref{thm:lambda-one} while analyzing the public
+\texttt{hodge\_data} dataset~\cite{LiuData26}, but could not
+identify the constants at the successive orders of the asymptotic
+expansion.
+GPT-6-Astra identified the constants but did not provide a proof.
+GPT-6.1-Sol supplied the proof and discovered and proved
+Theorems~\ref{thm:fixed-insertions}, \ref{thm:top-hodge}
+and~\ref{thm:fixed-defect}.
+
+GPT-6.1-Sol also wrote most of the manuscript. I wrote the initial
+draft of the Introduction, established the writing standards,
+designed the multi-agent writing workflow, and supervised
+GPT-6.1-Sol throughout the writing of the paper.
+
+The scholarly credit for this work should go to GPT-6.1-Sol.
+I release this paper solely for knowledge sharing and claim
+neither scholarly credit nor priority for this work.
+
+The results have not been formally verified in Lean and may
+contain errors. Readers should exercise caution and examine
+the arguments carefully.
